            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="BRO11" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>William Henry</forename>
                        <surname>Brooke</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1772">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1860"/>
                    <occupation>satirist and portrait painter</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Active in London from 1810 (although he diod not exhibit between 1813 and
                            1823). Connections to art circles. Most likely the Brooke of the 1830s,
                            but it is possible he was visiting Godwin in 1809. We have coded the
                            1830s accordingly - and with some confidence; but we also coded the 1809
                            Brookes - while recognising that this may be more questionable. There is
                            also an issue about how much weight to put on Godwin's distinction
                            between Brooke and Brookes, especially since the latter may be a
                            plural. However, we have treated these as distinct and coded them distinctly.  </p>
                    </note>
